{"units": [{"id": "aktaino-note2", "translation": "Schol. κουφίζειν [to lift up]. It also means γαυριᾶν [to prance] and ἀτάκτως πηδᾶν [to leap disorderly]. Phrynichus in Bekk. Anecd. p. 23, 12 ἀκταινῶσαι [to raise oneself] - Aeschylus says \"οὐκέτ᾽ ἀκταίνω\" [I no longer raise myself] with barytone accent, as if to say \"I can no longer hold myself upright.\""}, {"id": "aktaino-quote1", "translation": "so that I can neither stand firm nor lift my step,"}, {"id": "aktaino-quote2", "translation": "ἀκταινῶσαι [to raise oneself] - Aeschylus says \"οὐκέτ᾽ ἀκταίνω\" [I no longer raise myself] with barytone accent, as if to say \"I can no longer hold myself upright\""}, {"id": "aktaino-word1", "translation": "standing"}, {"id": "aktaino-word2", "translation": "to the corrector"}, {"id": "aktaino-word3", "translation": "written βάσιν [step]"}, {"id": "aktaino-word4", "translation": "to lift up. It also means to prance and to leap disorderly"}, {"id": "aktaion-orth1", "translation": "Actaeon"}, {"id": "aktaion-def1", "translation": "Actaeon."}, {"id": "aktaion-note1", "translation": "(in Bekk. Anecd. p. 351, 4)"}, {"id": "aktaion-note2", "translation": "where Ἀκταίων [Actaeon] is in the codex."}, {"id": "aktaion-quote1", "translation": "No day of the beast ever sent Actaeon to the house,"}, {"id": "aktaion-word1", "translation": "Actaeon"}, {"id": "akte-orth1", "translation": "shore"}, {"id": "akte-def1", "translation": "shore."}, {"id": "akte-def2", "translation": "mound."}, {"id": "akte-note1", "translation": "[Ag. 985 ψαμμίας ἀκάτα [sandy boat], where Ahrensius ψαμμὶς ἀκτά [sandy shore].]"}, {"id": "akte-quote1", "translation": "the shores of Salamis."}, {"id": "akte-quote2", "translation": "along the rugged shores."}, {"id": "akte-quote3", "translation": "the shores and reefs were full of corpses."}, {"id": "akte-quote4", "translation": "upon the sea shore."}, {"id": "akte-quote5", "translation": "around the shores of Cychreia."}, {"id": "akte-quote6", "translation": "and the ill-fated shore."}, {"id": "akte-quote7", "translation": "wandering on the shores (on the heights Weilius) of Salamis, striking the rugged shore."}, {"id": "akte-quote8", "translation": "to the leafy shores of Simois."}, {"id": "akte-quote9", "translation": "sandy boat,"}, {"id": "akte-quote10", "translation": "sandy shore"}, {"id": "akte-quote11", "translation": "to the ship-faring shores of Pallas."}, {"id": "akte-quote12", "translation": "around the shore of Cenaean Zeus."}, {"id": "akte-quote13", "translation": "I see this herald from the shore."}, {"id": "akte-quote14", "translation": "lady shore of the mound."}, {"id": "aktis-orth1", "translation": "ray"}, {"id": "aktis-def1", "translation": "ray."}, {"id": "aktis-quote1", "translation": "the sun looks upon with its rays."}, {"id": "aktis-quote2", "translation": "the sun blazing the earth with its rays,"}, {"id": "aktis-quote3", "translation": "before the god's rays are scattered."}, {"id": "aktis-quote4", "translation": "if any ray of the sun observes him."}, {"id": "aktor-orth1", "translation": "leader"}, {"id": "aktor-def1", "translation": "leader."}, {"id": "aktor-def2", "translation": "proper name."}, {"id": "aktor-quote1", "translation": "a leader dear to the Susians."}, {"id": "aktor-quote2", "translation": "leaders and champions of the Achaeans."}, {"id": "aktor-quote3", "translation": "Actor, brother of the aforementioned (Hyperbius)."}, {"id": "akymon-orth1", "translation": "not agitated by waves"}, {"id": "akymon-def1", "translation": "not agitated by waves."}, {"id": "akymon-quote1", "translation": "the waveless sea."}, {"id": "akon-orth1", "translation": "unwilling"}, {"id": "akon-def1", "translation": "unwilling."}, {"id": "akon-note1", "translation": "We have spoken about the trisyllabic form ἀέκων [unwilling] in its proper place."}, {"id": "akon-quote1", "translation": "I will nail you unwilling with unyielding bonds."}, {"id": "akon-quote2", "translation": "marrying an unwilling bride from an unwilling father."}, {"id": "akon-quote3", "translation": "he shut out of the house unwilling, unwilling."}, {"id": "akon-quote4", "translation": "you did not shout this unwillingly."}, {"id": "akon-quote5", "translation": "Zeus unwilling."}, {"id": "akon-quote6", "translation": "willing to share evils with the unwilling."}, {"id": "akon-quote7", "translation": "and it came to make them wise even against their will."}, {"id": "akon-word1", "translation": "unwilling"}, {"id": "alabastrophoros-orth1", "translation": "carrying alabaster boxes"}, {"id": "alabastrophoros-def1", "translation": "carrying alabaster boxes."}, {"id": "alabastrophoros-quote1", "translation": "Aeschylus (fr. 354) called the one carrying alabaster boxes alabastrophoros."}, {"id": "aletheia_see-orth1", "translation": "truth"}, {"id": "aletheia_see-word1", "translation": "truth"}, {"id": "alathes_see-orth1", "translation": "true"}, {"id": "alathes_see-word1", "translation": "true"}, {"id": "alaino-orth1", "translation": "wander about"}, {"id": "alaino-def1", "translation": "wander about."}, {"id": "alaino-note1", "translation": "[αλαιός [wandering] erroneously for αλεός [distraught], which see.]"}, {"id": "alaino-quote1", "translation": "a dream appearing by day wanders,"}, {"id": "alaino-word1", "translation": "wandering"}, {"id": "alaino-word2", "translation": "distraught"}, {"id": "alalazo-orth1", "translation": "utter a sound"}, {"id": "alalazo-def1", "translation": "utter a sound."}, {"id": "alalazo-quote1", "translation": "the twang resounds."}, {"id": "alalos-orth1", "translation": "mute"}, {"id": "alalos-def1", "translation": "mute."}, {"id": "alalos-note1", "translation": "(in the scholia to Arist. Av. 277)"}, {"id": "alalos-quote1", "translation": "Who is this prophet of the Muses, mute?"}, {"id": "alalos-word1", "translation": "walking delicately"}, {"id": "alaomai-orth1", "translation": "wander about"}, {"id": "alaomai-def1", "translation": "wander about."}, {"id": "alaomai-quote1", "translation": "to wander free to the farthest bounds of the earth."}, {"id": "alaomai-quote2", "translation": "having wandered to the sandy mound of Sarpedon."}, {"id": "alaomai-quote3", "translation": "for now we are somehow wandering, having been sold."}, {"id": "alaomai-quote4", "translation": "and I wander shamefully."}, {"id": "alaos-orth1", "translation": "blind"}, {"id": "alaos-def1", "translation": "blind."}, {"id": "alaos-quote1", "translation": "the blind race of men."}, {"id": "alaos-quote2", "translation": "punishment for the blind and the seeing,"}, {"id": "alapazo-orth1", "translation": "destroy"}, {"id": "alapazo-def1", "translation": "destroy."}, {"id": "alapazo-note1", "translation": "where Triclinius Μοίρα λαπάξει [Fate will destroy], which form Aeschylus uses elsewhere when the meter demands."}, {"id": "alapazo-quote1", "translation": "and all the flocks of the towers - Fate will destroy,"}, {"id": "alapazo-word1", "translation": "Fate will destroy"}, {"id": "alastoros_see-orth1", "translation": "avenging deity"}, {"id": "alastoros_see-word1", "translation": "avenging deity"}, {"id": "alastos-orth1", "translation": "pernicious"}, {"id": "alastos-def1", "translation": "pernicious."}, {"id": "alastos-quote1", "translation": "unforgettable, hateful, and harmful things."}, {"id": "alastor-orth1", "translation": "avenging deity"}, {"id": "alastor-def1", "translation": "avenging deity."}, {"id": "alastor-def2", "translation": "a man pursued by divine vengeance."}]}